# Staging auto-push

When the user asks for product/code changes in this repo:

1. Implement the change.
2. Unless they explicitly say not to commit/push: create a git commit and `git push` to `origin` (usually `main`) so Railway/Vercel staging update.
3. Follow the repo git commit protocol (status/diff/log, HEREDOC message, no secrets, no force push).
4. After push, remind them briefly if a DB migration is needed (`npx prisma migrate deploy` on Railway) when a new Prisma migration was included.
5. Do not push unrelated local WIP; only the files for the completed request.
